-- title:
--   Degree of the q↦ q^ℓ degeneracy map on ℚ(j(qᵈ):d∣ N)
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and $\ell$ a prime. For a nonzero $M$, `modularFunctionFieldFull M` is the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \mathbb{Q}((q))$ (Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$) generated by the set of all `qExpand ℚ d jq` with $d$ a nonzero divisor of $M$, that is, by the substituted $j$-expansions $j(q^{d})$, where `qExpand R d` is the ring endomorphism of Laurent series obtained by pushing the exponent lattice forward along multiplication by $d$ on $\mathbb{Z}$ (the substitution $q \mapsto q^{d}$). The theorem concerns the image of `modularFunctionFieldFull N` under the $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra map `qExpandₐ ℓ`, i.e. the field $\mathbb{Q}\bigl(j(q^{\ell d}) : d \mid N\bigr)$, viewed inside the larger field `modularFunctionFieldFull (N * ℓ)` $= \mathbb{Q}\bigl(j(q^{e}) : e \mid N\ell\bigr)$. It asserts that the relative degree `IntermediateField.relfinrank` of the first in the second (these being nested, the degree of the second over the first) equals $\ell$ when $\ell \mid N$ and $\ell + 1$ otherwise.
--
--   This is the function-field form of the degree of the second degeneracy map $X_0(N\ell) \to X_0(N)$, namely $\psi(N\ell)/\psi(N)$ for Dedekind's $\psi$. Together with the inclusion coming from the first degeneracy map it provides the degree data used in the treatment of the Hecke correspondence $T_\ell$ at level $N$, and it is cited by the computations of `finrankAlong` for the degeneracy and Hecke maps, among them [`ModularCurve.finrankAlong_heckeBetaBar`](thm.html#ModularCurve.finrankAlong_heckeBetaBar).
